WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:02.540
- [Narrator] The North
Korean leader Kim Jong-un

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:04.360
has been busy since the country started

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:05.580
its first major battle

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.250
against a COVID-19 outbreak in May.

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:11.410
He's personally inspected
pharmacies in Pyongyang.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.110
Kim visited the country's Headquarters

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.554
for Epidemic Prevention,

00:00:14.554 --> 00:00:16.300
and he's held numerous meetings

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.020
where he berated officials for failing

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:20.630
to prevent the public health crisis.

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:22.050
Pyongyang officially announced

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:23.730
its first locally transmitted case

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:25.920
more than two years into the pandemic

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.990
and since then, hundreds of thousands

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.100
of what North Korea calls fever cases

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.966
have been reported daily.

00:00:31.966 --> 00:00:32.799
- This is really eye-opening

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:35.360
that Kim Jong-un would
say it's the worst crisis

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:37.500
since the foundation of the country.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.780
- [Narrator] Examining Kim's
recent pandemic policies

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.860
and public service announcements help

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:44.080
to understand what resources are available

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:46.148
in the country, as well as what's lacking

00:00:46.148 --> 00:00:49.003
as the regime attempts
to stamp out the virus.

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:52.210
In the early days of the pandemic,

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:53.950
North Korea closed its borders,

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:55.670
including a shoot-on-sight order

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:57.470
for people attempting to cross it.

00:00:57.470 --> 00:00:59.600
And it worked to keep the virus at bay.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:01.490
But now with the surge in cases fueled

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:03.560
by the fast-spreading Omicron variant,

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:05.500
the country is taking new measures.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:06.720
- The message has sort of been

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:09.522
to convince people that the leadership

00:01:09.522 --> 00:01:11.310
is working very hard for them.

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:12.610
- [Narrator] One of the first acts

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:14.970
was to order the lockdown of major cities.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:17.810
Still, Pyongyang has
reported more than 60 deaths

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:20.230
and over three million fever cases.

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:21.310
- Case of fever,

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:24.403
that's essentially a
euphemism for coronavirus.

00:01:24.403 --> 00:01:27.210
They have very limited testing capacity.

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:28.500
The World Health Organization

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:30.860
has said since the start of the pandemic,

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:34.690
North Korea has tested
about 64,000 people.

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:37.430
That works out at less than 100 a day.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:38.770
- [Narrator] The lack of testing capacity

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:40.170
is one of the major challenges

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:42.140
in the country's battle against the virus.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:45.060
- If you're trying to
do a lockdown strategy,

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:47.270
you need to be testing people as well

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:49.080
to be able to tell when
it's safe for people

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.150
to come out.

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:52.070
- [Narrator] With mass
testing not an option,

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:53.690
the leader has looked for other measures

00:01:53.690 --> 00:01:55.520
to tackle the crisis.

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:57.000
Kim has mobilized the military

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.850
to help ensure basic medical supplies

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:00.790
are available in the capital city

00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:03.020
where the first cases were reported.

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:04.440
Crews donning hazmat suits

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:07.640
have been disinfecting
streets, factories and stores.

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:10.430
- People in Pyongyang have
been encouraged to wear masks.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:14.990
We've even seen Kim Jong-un
himself wearing two masks.

00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:18.400
And we did go to the border
area between South Korea

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.830
and North Korea, and we could
see people walking around

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:24.570
on the North Korean side
who were not wearing masks.

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:27.830
So the presence of masks seems

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:32.190
to be not complete across
the country at least.

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:36.670
Perhaps the availability of
masks is one reason for that.

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:38.490
- [Narrator] Kim's actions
have also been accompanied

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:41.008
by public health segments
on state television.

00:02:41.008 --> 00:02:42.580
(host speaking in foreign language)

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:44.300
In this segment, a presenter explained

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:47.640
how to take painkillers
like paracetamol for fevers.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:49.380
- To our knowledge,
they don't have supplies

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:52.550
of antiviral medicines, which treat COVID.

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:54.800
What they're looking at
to treat these things

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:56.550
is sort of basic medicines

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:59.970
but if someone's got severe
breathing difficulties,

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:02.190
it's obviously not sufficient.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:03.710
- [Narrator] Another
segment advised viewers

00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:05.323
to wash hands regularly,

00:03:06.469 --> 00:03:09.030
nurses to wear masks,

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:11.910
and that those with fever should isolate.

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:13.360
But one of the most effective ways

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.030
to combat the virus has been missing

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:16.690
from these public service announcements

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:18.430
and other COVID policies,

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:20.350
and that's to get vaccinated.

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:22.790
That's because there's no
known vaccines available

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:23.910
in North Korea.

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:25.960
And the country has also rejected doses

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:27.530
from the World Health Organization

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:28.710
and South Korea.

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:30.370
But recently, it's reached out to one

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:32.090
of its closest allies for help.

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:35.840
- There have been flights
by North Korean cargo planes

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:38.850
from China bringing in medical supplies,

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:39.900
quite secretly actually.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:40.970
They haven't announced this.

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:43.430
I don't think they want
to let their people know

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:46.150
that they're relying on another country

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:48.130
to provide supplies.

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:49.980
- [Narrator] Health experts
say that without vaccines

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:51.420
and testing capacity,

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:53.410
North Korea risks being overwhelmed

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:54.910
by a health crisis not seen

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:56.770
since the country suffered a famine

00:03:56.770 --> 00:03:59.930
that killed over a million
people in the 1990s.

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:02.120
The population is particularly vulnerable

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:04.230
because of widespread malnutrition,

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:07.160
and the decrepit state of
the country's medical system.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:10.080
In rural areas, hospitals
are reported to lack supplies

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:12.972
and some even operate without electricity.

00:04:12.972 --> 00:04:15.860
- If the provinces and rural areas

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:17.310
are more badly affected,

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:19.530
which is where we see more malnutrition,

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:21.460
I would say that this
is probably not going

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:23.330
to trouble the regime too much

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:26.300
because this is something
that we saw in the past

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.140
during the famine of the 1990s

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:31.250
but if the casualty rate is very high

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.420
in the capital in Pyongyang,

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:35.170
that's potentially de-stabilizing

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:38.310
because that's where the
leadership relies on the people

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:40.880
for their support in order
to keep the Kim family

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.800
and Kim Jong-un specifically in power.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:45.770
- [Narrator] But the pandemic
isn't the only big task

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:46.840
on Kim's plate.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:48.860
As he enters the second
decade of his rule,

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:50.180
the regime faces sanctions

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:52.140
that have battered the country's economy

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:54.240
and it continues to move
aggressively forward

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.161
with frequent weapons tests.

00:04:56.161 --> 00:04:57.360
(booming sound)

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:58.900
- [Alastair] Those things require

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:02.030
a large amount of attention
from the leadership.

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:03.820
Can they multitask?

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:05.259
That's the big question.

00:05:05.259 --> 00:05:07.927
(dramatic music)

